<p>KRA's eTIMS needs every sale to be sent to a control unit registered to your KRA PIN and branch. In <strong>Settings → Integrations → KRA eTIMS</strong>, add each branch's device with the TIN, branch ID and serial number KRA gave you, and initialise it.</p>

<ul>
  <li>Products are registered with KRA the first time they're sold at that branch.</li>
  <li>Each sale, void and return is sent to KRA, and KRA's signature and QR code are printed on the receipt.</li>
  <li>If KRA can't be reached, the sale goes ahead and is queued. HardPoint keeps retrying, and <strong>eTIMS → Submissions</strong> shows anything still waiting.</li>
</ul>

<p>Set each tax rate's eTIMS code, and the item class of your categories, so KRA classifies your goods correctly.</p>
